quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  8,17,"So you did not kill them, but it was Allah who killed them. And (Esteemed Prophet,) you did not throw (the handful of sand and pebbles at your enemies) when you threw (at the outset of the battle of Badr); instead, it was Allah Who threw, that He might try the believers with a beautiful trial from Himself. Indeed, Allah is All-Hearing, All-Knowing."
  8,18,"That is (what you are granted), and Allah indeed weakens the strategy of the disbelievers."
  8,19,"(O Meccan disbelievers!) If you were seeking victory, then the (decision of) victory has already come to you. If you stop here, it would be better for you. And if you return (to fighting), We shall also return. And your troops, though greater in number, shall avail you nothing. And (know) that Allah is with the believers."
  8,20,"O believers! Obey Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and do not turn away from him while you are listening (to him)."
  8,21,"And do not be like those who say: ‘We hear,’ but they do not listen."
  8,22,"Indeed, the worst of all creatures in Allah’s sight are those who are (wilfully) the deaf and the dumb who do not understand."
  8,23,"Had Allah known any virtue in them, He would have surely made them hear. But even if He had made them hear, they would still have turned away, not taking any notice (of the truth)."
  8,24,"O believers! Respond to (the call of) Allah and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) whenever he calls you to that which gives you (everlasting) life. Know that Allah intervenes between a man and (the desires of) his heart, and towards Him, you will all be gathered."
  8,25,And guard yourselves against affliction (of temptation) which shall befall not only those among you who are wrongdoers. And know that Allah is severe in retribution.
